qfdevd (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix qfdevd failing to start on a fresh install. With ProtectSystem=strict,
    systemd only sets up the ReadWritePaths=-/config/quartzfire writable bind
    when that directory already exists at namespace construction; on a fresh
    install it does not, so /config was read-only inside the daemon's namespace
    and its create_dir_all() failed with EROFS — the daemon exited before
    signalling READY and the unit restart-looped. Add a privileged, mount-aware
    `qfdevd init-store` step (ExecStartPre=+…) that creates the dir group-
    writable before the sandboxed main process starts.

 -- QuartzFire <cwellman@quartz.systems>  Tue, 14 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

qfdevd (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: device/client monitoring for QuartzFire.
    - Neighbor-table collector (ip -j neigh) driving online/offline status.
    - Kea DHCPv4 lease collector (memfile CSV) with static-reservation
      detection from the Kea config.
    - conntrack byte accounting (snapshot + DESTROY-event stream) into 5-minute
      usage buckets for 1h/24h/7d windows.
    - MAC OUI vendor lookup + DHCP-hostname device-type/OS fingerprinting.
    - Shared SQLite inventory (WAL) at /config/quartzfire/devices.db read by the
      WebUI backend (Monitoring - Devices).

 -- QuartzFire <cwellman@quartz.systems>  Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
